{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"98183443699060a30d2388003e2d98e9a206dac684669f8cb84fec0f9dd9113e","slug":"crocodash.projects.ocean-only","location":"/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Project: Ocean Only Configuration - The Bare Minimum","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"CrocoDash","language":"python"},"github":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery/blob/main/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","edit_url":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery/edit/main/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"ocean_only.ipynb","url":"/CrocoGallery/latest/build/ocean_only-48c781f6d835a93fa2c7429ec59286aa.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This project is all about how we create the most basic ocean_only domain to shake things out and get spinning as fast as possible. This is one way of testing everything before we get into our research questions.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"PVycnqfDpi"}],"key":"vLTofGBDPb"}],"identifier":"84b4b4ad","html_id":"84b4b4ad","key":"udGTMIFXpr"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download this project by either:","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"OmHmdOvP9z"}],"key":"VQYYJHuV6s"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running the CrocoDash CLI command: ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"dzAKin3108"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crocodash template --output ocean_only_case.ipynb --machine glade --notebook crocodash.projects.ocean_only","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"FKRxwXaOU1"},{"type":"text","value":", then filling in the paths it leaves as placeholders","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"WnJGoPQHqF"}],"key":"w05yCIvHOg"}],"key":"iNOyDdemsX"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copying the file from your CrocoDash checkout: ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"TB7B11jR38"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gallery/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"CFqNBcVaeO"}],"key":"G0J8AJfixR"}],"key":"V5D9f9SSpm"}],"key":"eWQOF62VA1"}],"identifier":"d75d080e","html_id":"d75d080e","key":"onV7c2F897"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grid Generation","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"fim3h2i3SQ"}],"identifier":"grid-generation","label":"Grid Generation","html_id":"grid-generation","implicit":true,"key":"e45XprbKJ9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first thing we are going to do is think about how to get a domain. Scaling data is available online, but a 100x100 point domain is relatively quick. If we provide ~40 cores for the ocean, it’ll run within a few minutes.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Hy8vPhR5rr"}],"key":"u7cc0gqldO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll pick a 100x100 point horizontal grid and a standard vertical grid.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"iLWlHN9Zam"}],"key":"szR8hf7SFs"}],"identifier":"e0fc8055","html_id":"e0fc8055","key":"Yj6M3YRDTD"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from CrocoDash.grid import Grid\nfrom CrocoDash.vgrid import VGrid\n\ngrid = Grid(\n  resolution = 0.05, # in degrees\n  xstart = 278.0, # min longitude in [0, 360]\n  lenx = 5.0, # longitude extent in degrees\n  ystart = 7.0, # min latitude in [-90, 90]\n  leny = 5.0, # latitude extent in degrees\n  name = \"basic_grid\",\n)\n\n\nvgrid  = VGrid.hyperbolic(\n    nk = 75, # number of vertical levels\n    depth = 2000,\n    ratio=20.0 # target ratio of top to bottom layer thicknesses\n)","key":"vWRsL7Aas4"},{"type":"outputs","id":"vrdbFmOEAFmpqJfaJdWhT","children":[],"key":"N8UxdzlldH"}],"identifier":"0325b73d","html_id":"0325b73d","key":"ifnnycoEQl"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now that we have our horizontal and vertical grids, we need to setup our bathymetry. Normally, we’d use the ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"rjKsZpbYuf"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Topo.set_from_dataset","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"prA6w996zK"},{"type":"text","value":" function to go from a bathymetry dataset to grid bathymetry. However, as a first step we’ll skip the dataset entirely and use an idealized bathymetry. ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"FWUUW767E1"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Topo","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"dEeDR1euGT"},{"type":"text","value":" provides helpers mirroring MOM6’s built-in TOPO_CONFIG options, such as ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"XHFnDBrn4R"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spoon","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"DQZ5GUs1NY"},{"type":"text","value":", the analytic basin shape used in MOM6’s idealized double gyre case.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"TVy1CI3uUz"}],"key":"cq7slEWcDo"}],"identifier":"35338f50","html_id":"35338f50","key":"SxH07KFq5Y"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from CrocoDash.topo import Topo\n\ntopo = Topo(\n    grid = grid,\n    min_depth = 9.5, # in meters\n)\n\ntopo.set_spoon(max_depth = 2000, dedge = 200)\n\ntopo.depth.plot()","key":"tVyZXI69xL"},{"type":"outputs","id":"I9Oxa5X9QWe51keu6NsKp","children":[],"key":"uUQYEwyCyZ"}],"identifier":"664779d2","html_id":"664779d2","key":"e4Ew2w3Hya"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Great! So I’m going to create my case now, and this step will hardly ever change!","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"NQjvekhg4c"}],"key":"GJFc30UROs"}],"identifier":"4e386f52","html_id":"4e386f52","key":"Q6BIkyA4re"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom CrocoDash.case import Case\n\n# CESM case (experiment) name\ncasename = \"basic_ocean\"\n\n# CESM source root (Update this path accordingly!!!)\ncesmroot =\"<CESM>\"\n\n# Place where all your input files go \ninputdir = Path(\"<inputdir>\") / casename\n    \n# CESM case directory\ncaseroot = Path(\"<casedir>\") / casename\n\n\ncase = Case(\n    cesmroot = cesmroot,\n    caseroot = caseroot,\n    inputdir = inputdir,\n    ocn_grid = grid,\n    ocn_vgrid = vgrid,\n    ocn_topo = topo,\n    project = \"<PROJECT>\", # Update this with your project code\n    job_queue = \"<JOB_QUEUE>\", # PBS queue the run is submitted to\n    job_wallclock_time = \"<WALLCLOCK_1H>\", # hh:mm:ss walltime requested for the run\n    override = True,\n    machine = \"derecho\",\n    compset = \"CR_JRA\"\n)","key":"Q54fd6zk4F"},{"type":"outputs","id":"UN5duwH5JjcRabHIejv1W","children":[],"key":"Wm76qjLNun"}],"identifier":"ca45d4f1","html_id":"ca45d4f1","key":"XlPKiLNKF7"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now, the last step is to generate forcings, which is done as a two step configure and process. Since it can take a long time to get raw data from outside sources, we’re going to use a fake data generator that comes with CrocoDash.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"pLopYl76qf"}],"key":"NBgzu0FBs1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I also think we can run for 60 days. That doesn’t sound too bad.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"hlb6iTkBri"}],"key":"ihDZgJVinZ"}],"identifier":"44b97111","html_id":"44b97111","key":"tMuueHfDqC"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"case.configure_forcings(\n    date_range = [\"2019-01-01 00:00:00\", \"2019-03-03 00:00:00\"],\n    product_name=\"reference_ocean\",\n    function_name=\"get_reference_ocean_data\"\n)\n","key":"pVijvQChW8"},{"type":"outputs","id":"m3yNAlgi26uLC3PvXtPsD","children":[],"key":"CSO2rfme6b"}],"identifier":"7ff41626","html_id":"7ff41626","key":"sUsCyU2Rim"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"case.process_forcings()\n","key":"BcJzjcos2J"},{"type":"outputs","id":"CASP1FnqxLJAFVF5bUdY6","children":[],"key":"gtGjBYdggv"}],"identifier":"890857d3","html_id":"890857d3","key":"l6AdyaPUxj"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cool! Once this is done, we have to ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"ZMzCIjaQJI"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"./case.build","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"ZEO9IgrBiX"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Pbnfr36bIK"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"./case.submit","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"o2x9IT2ujP"},{"type":"text","value":" in our case directory. Before that though, here’s some things I’d ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"lZfuhghAjR"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xmlchange","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"bnqHQ9FqGH"},{"type":"text","value":" to make the domain run faster.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"sSgy42XITH"}],"key":"MVxLyZwtQp"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"mcjC70adYI"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NTASKS = 10","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"VvoE9D5v6q"},{"type":"text","value":", which sets every component to 10 cores, and makes the data atmosphere regridding very fast. (All components share these 10 cores)","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"EpOeaAT3au"}],"key":"uQ5lj5rHIi"}],"key":"dhm4xvntTE"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"Sdhe3pFTwl"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NTASKS_OCN = 40","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"Kukve0mWgb"},{"type":"text","value":" because of the scaling data we saw: ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"LgUGMcgMpT"},{"type":"link","url":"https://crocodile-cesm.github.io/SeaSloth/mom6_scaling.html","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://​crocodile​-cesm​.github​.io​/SeaSloth​/mom6​_scaling​.html","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"LQ3YIgGS4D"}],"urlSource":"https://crocodile-cesm.github.io/SeaSloth/mom6_scaling.html","key":"o93Nrz1IBo"}],"key":"hFYCGBc8i1"}],"key":"zOqaGyBZrw"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"IUwakniFcj"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ROOTPE = 0","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"KktwQ5tE4J"},{"type":"text","value":", which ensures that all components share the same cores. If I set ROOTPE_OCN=10, it would skip the first 10 cores and run on the next 40 cores.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"dTsINNv9yo"}],"key":"E8FxcY9Nft"}],"key":"vY19InLrpv"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"ewXt7ha421"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JOB_WALLCLOCK_TIME = 00:30:00 --subgroup case.run","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"QU7WDY1aPg"},{"type":"text","value":", which ensures the queue picks up our job realllly fast.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"OEIBd7DWP5"}],"key":"NoyLYoW28a"}],"key":"tSTlUOMomn"}],"key":"KZ7OcTaUvL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And there we go! A fake running ocean model! Isn’t that awesome!","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"O2a1bEQx9k"}],"key":"EM5nwgoUVb"}],"identifier":"6fa10400","html_id":"6fa10400","key":"PGpPbi0WDh"}],"key":"LwDS5HrdQC"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"CROCODILE 2026 Workshop Projects","short_title":"Projects","url":"/crocodash/projects","group":"Use Cases"},"next":{"title":"Project: CICE Configuration - Ayy, It’s Chilly!","url":"/crocodash/projects/cice","group":"Use Cases"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}